From 1a6f26062b218ce135b4bae600acd5998c92e050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0xFFshell <0xffshell@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:23:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Take the water bucket out on the way down

MovementFall was the last place in the mod that put an item in the hand
itself and clicked on the same tick: it selected the water bucket when the
destination came within reach, and the click went the tick the crosshair
landed. That is the same bypass Tempo fixed for the Elytra firework - an
item appearing in the hand out of nowhere, with the item that would be used
not necessarily the one that was decided on.

The bucket is now asked for through InventoryBehavior#hold from the first
airborne tick of a fall that will need one, so the two-to-five-tick beat is
spent on the way down, in the air, where nothing is waiting on it. That is
also what a person does: nobody arrives at the ground holding the bucket
they only thought about halfway. The click then waits for the hand the way
every other click does.

The direct selection stays, as the landing guarantee underneath the beat:
if the crosshair reaches the spot before the hand does, the bucket goes into
it on that tick rather than the water being missed. It costs nothing in the
ordinary case - an ask that is already in hand is dropped, and the behaviour
that presses hotbar keys runs between the ask and the click, so the click
still goes out on the tick it would have - and a fall that would have been
caught on that tick still is. The pickup after the landing goes through the
beat as well, and prefers the empty bucket already in the hand rather than
switching to a different one.

HandWritesTest counts the writes, the way CameraWritesTest counts camera
writes: the selected slot may be written in the beat and in the fall's
landing guarantee and nowhere else, and the shapes of both are pinned. It
has teeth - a probe file with setSelectedSlot( in it fails the count, a
comment mentioning it does not - and it exists because this rule had already
been forgotten twice.

Validation: ./gradlew :test - 291 tests, 0 failures.
---
